<title>MEXICO: GMexico gives copper output breakdown for 1996.</title>
<headline>GMexico gives copper output breakdown for 1996.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's largest copper producer Grupo Mexico, known as GMexico, gave a breakdown of its copper output seen for 1996.</p>
<p>In an interview, Deputy Finance Director Carlos Oyanguren said production this year would be around 340,000 copper content tonnes up 10 percent compared to last year. He gave the following breakdown.</p>
<p>    Location			    Volume	 Copper Type</p>
<p>    San Luis Potosi smelter	 40,000	    Anode</p>
<p>    La Caridad smelter	     180,000	    Anode</p>
<p>    La Caridad SX-EW		  22,000	   Cathode</p>
<p>    Cananea smelter		@  60,000	   Blister</p>
<p>    Cananea SX-EW		     35,000	   Cathode</p>
<p>    Total			    @ 347,000	     N/A</p>
<p>Legend - Volumes in tonnes. The sign for Cananea smelter signifies output will be up to that level but not above and so the total is also approximate.</p>
<p>--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom (525) 7289530. E-mail at chris.aspin@reuters.com</p>
